[71.961592, "i", "cat /app/task/instruction.md\n"]
[71.962578, "o", "cat /app/task/instruction.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[71.962609, "o", "# Post-Compromise Forensic Investigation and Remediation Planning\r\n\r\nYou are a DFIR analyst working on an **analysis machine** — **not** the compromised server.\r\nA read-only forensic copy of the host is mounted at `/disk`, and the output of the\r\nsecurity product (alerts, vulnerability scan, baseline checks) is at `/sas`.\r\n\r\n## Scenario\r\n\r\nAn unpatched Windows 10 host was exploited over SMBv1 using EternalBlue (CVE-2017-0144 / MS17-010). The attacker dumped LSASS, deployed ransomware, and established WMI event-subscription and DLL-hijack persistence, then cleared the System event log. Alerts surface the exploit implant, the LSASS dump, and the ransomware; the WMI subscription, the hijacked DLL, and the cleared log are silent.\r\n\r\n## Rules (load-bearing — do not violate)\r\n\r\n- You are on an analysis machine, not the compromised host.\r\n- `/disk` is a **read-only** forensic copy. Do not attempt to modify it.\r\n- Do **not** SSH into any machine or execute remediation — you are producing a plan, not\r\n  running it.\r\n- Every finding must be based on evidence in `/disk` or `/sas`.\r\n- Do **not** fabricate CVEs. State confidence levels when unsure.\r\n- In the remediation plan, prefer backup/quarantine over deletion.\r\n\r\n## Evidence is messy and multi-format\r\n\r\nReal disks are not clean text. Evidence is spread across log files, CSV/TSV tables, JSON\r\ntelemetry, config files, registry hives, `.evtx` event logs, inert binary samples, and\r\nmarkup — some of it rotated, gzipped, truncated at a cleared window, or partially\r\noverwritten. Use the right tool: `grep`/`rg`, `strings` (and `strings -e l` for UTF-16 in\r\nhives/event logs), `zcat` for `*.gz`, `jq` for JSON, `xxd` for raw bytes, `pdftotext` for\r\nPDFs. Indicators of compromise in provided intel are **defanged** (`hxxp://`, `evil[.]com`,\r\n`stratum+tcp[:]//`) — re-fang them mentally when correlating.\r\n\r\nBesides `/disk` (the host image) and the machine-readable feeds in `/sas`,\r\n`/sas` also carries analyst materials: `/sas/cti/` — a vendor threat advisory\r\n(text, PDF, and page-image PNGs) mapping the campaign to MITRE ATT&CK techniques and any\r\nrelevant CVEs; and `/sas/handoff/` — a **pre-filled change ticket with stale/incorrect\r\nentries to reconcile in place**, a findings JSON schema, and an incident intake form. Map your\r\non-disk findings to the advisory's ATT&CK claims, and correct the change ticket against your\r\nown evidence rather than trusting it.\r\n\r\n## Citations (required)\r\n\r\nEvery finding in every report must be followed by a **backtick-delimited** citation of the\r\nform `` `/absolute/path` `` or `` `/absolute/path:line` `` pointing at evidence under\r\n`/disk` **or** `/sas`. Use `/sas` for findings whose only evidence is\r\nan alert — e.g. a network connection, or an event whose primary log was wiped. **Findings\r\nwithout a resolvable citation will not be credited.**\r\n\r\n## Deliverables\r\n\r\nWrite all five files to `/app`. A run that produces fewer than five is scored as\r\nincomplete, not as a low score.\r\n\r\n| File | Content |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `progress.md` | Investigation timeline and working checklist |\r\n| `intrusion-report.md` | Attack chain, evidence, entities, persistence, impact |\r\n| `vuln-report.md` | Vulnerability-driven entry analysis (or its explicit absence) |\r\n| `baseline-report.md` | Baseline / configuration weaknesses |\r\n| `remediation-plan.md` | Prioritised, correct, complete, verifiable plan |\r\n\r\nDetection and remediation are scored on **separate** axes. Investigate the whole host — the\r\nalerts do not cover everything that happened.\r\n"]
[71.963072, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@fadb0ad66d2f:/app/task# "]
[77.208582, "i", "cat /app/task/tests/structure/required_sections.py\n"]
[77.208888, "o", "cat /app/task/tests/structure/required_sections.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[77.209864, "o", "# tests/structure/required_sections.py  (FIXED — structure gate, required_pass)\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\n"]
[77.209972, "o", "import rewardkit as rk\r\nfrom rewardkit import criterion\r\n\r\n# Minimal section contract each report must satisfy (case-insensitive substring match).\r\n# Deliberately loose — the gate checks SHAPE, not content quality. In particular it does NOT\r\n# require verification language in the plan (that is a Tier-1 plan score, not a structure\r\n# gate), so a well-formed but evidence-free no-op report still passes structure.\r\n# Each requirement is either a substring that must appear, or a tuple of alternatives of which\r\n# at least one must appear. This is a SHAPE gate only. The intrusion report must contain an\r\n# attack-chain section (the entry point is its first step); it is NOT additionally required to\r\n# contain the literal word \"entry\" — the instruction asks for \"attack chain, evidence, entities,\r\n# persistence, impact\", and a report that names the entry via a MITRE technique such as\r\n# \"Exploitation of Remote Services (T1210)\" or \"Initial Access\" must not fail a shape check.\r\n# Entry-point QUALITY is scored on the detection axis (chain step 1 / discovery), not here.\r\nREQUIRED_SECTIONS = {\r\n    \"intrusion-report.md\": (\"chain\",),                # attack chain (entry point = its step 1)\r\n    \"vuln-report.md\":      (\"vuln\",),                 # a vulnerability section\r\n    \"baseline-report.md\":  (\"baseline\",),             # baseline weaknesses\r\n    \"remediation-plan.md\": (\"remediat\",),             # a remediation plan\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _headings(text: str) -> str:\r\n    return \"\\n\".join(l for l in text.splitlines() if l.lstrip().startswith(\"#\")).lower()\r\n\r\n\r\n@criterion(description=\"each report contains its required sections\", required_pass=True)\r\ndef required_sections(workspace: Path) -> bool:\r\n    for name, needles in REQUIRED_SECTIONS.items():\r\n        p = workspace / name\r\n        if not p.exists():\r\n            return False\r\n        blob = p.read_text(errors=\"replace\").lower()\r\n        heads = _headings(blob)\r\n        for n in needles:\r\n            alts = (n,) if isinstance(n, str) else n\r\n            if not any(a in heads or a in blob for a in alts):\r\n                return False\r\n    return True\r\n"]
[77.210015, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@fadb0ad66d2f:/app/task# "]
[84.120436, "i", "cat /app/task/tests/grounding/citations_resolve.py /app/task/tests/detection/no_cve_claimed.py\n"]
[84.121139, "o", "cat /app/task/tests/grounding/citations_resolve.py /app/task/tests/detection/no_cve_claimed.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[84.121432, "o", "# tests/grounding/citations_resolve.py  (FIXED — Tier 1, the evidence sub-score)\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport rewardkit as rk\r\nfrom rewardkit import criterion\r\n\r\n\r\n@criterion(description=\"fraction of findings whose citation resolves under /disk or /sas\")\r\ndef grounding_rate(workspace: Path) -> float:\r\n    \"\"\"Evidence sub-score, computed without a judge (doc 02 §2.3). A finding is grounded if\r\n    at least one of its citations resolves to a real file under an evidence root. Findings\r\n    whose citations are only 'plausible' (wrong file in a real dir) score 0 here but are not\r\n    fabrication; fabrication is handled by no_fabrication.py.\"\"\"\r\n    findings = rk.shared._findings(workspace)\r\n    if not findings:\r\n        return 0.0\r\n    classify = rk.shared._grounding(workspace)\r\n    grounded = 0\r\n    for f in findings:\r\n        if any(classify(path) == \"resolved\" for path, _ in f[\"citations\"]):\r\n            grounded += 1\r\n    return grounded / len(findings)\r\n# tests/detection/no_cve_claimed.py  (FIXED — Tier 1, the negative deliverable)\r\nimport re\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport rewardkit as rk\r\nfrom rewardkit import criterion\r\n\r\nCVE = re.compile(r\"cve-\\d{4}-\\d{4,7}\")\r\nNEGATED = (\"no cve\", \"not cve\", \"no known cve\", \"ruled out\", \"rather than\",\r\n           \"not driven by\", \"no vulnerability-driven\", \"not vulnerability-driven\",\r\n           \"no software vulnerability\", \"excluded\", \"is not\", \"no exploited\",\r\n           # an analyst rejects a planted / false CVE (Delta-2 reconciliation) with these too\r\n           \"false\", \"incorrect\", \"whereas\", \"not applicable\", \"n/a\", \"does not apply\",\r\n           \"rejected\", \"reject\", \"not exploited\", \"unrelated\", \"does not\", \"no rdp\",\r\n           \"not the entry\", \"not relevant\", \"cannot apply\", \"disproven\", \"invalid\", \"refuted\")\r\nCONCLUDES_NONE = (\"no cve\", \"not cve-driven\", \"no vulnerability-driven entry\",\r\n                  \"misconfiguration rather than\", \"no known cve\", \"no software vulnerability\",\r\n                  \"0 cves\", \"no cves\", \"none (0\", \"0 cve\", \"cve: none\",\r\n                  \"exploited: none\", \"exploited for entry: none\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@criterion(description=\"vuln-report correctly concludes no CVE-driven entry\")\r\ndef no_false_cve(workspace: Path, tag) -> float:\r\n    \"\"\"The negative-deliverable check. `tag` is a required scheduling marker: it forces this\r\n    criterion to be registered EXPLICITLY (build.py emits `rk.no_false_cve(...)` only for\r\n    no-CVE ranges) rather than auto-scheduled, so a CVE range never contributes a free 1.0 to\r\n    the detection axis. A CVE id is a false attribution only when asserted affirmatively —\r\n    naming a CVE to rule it out (\"entry was weak creds, not CVE-2021-44228\") is correct, not\r\n    fabrication (doc 04 §6).\"\"\"\r\n    m = rk.shared._manifest(workspace)\r\n    if not m.get(\"no_cve_entry\"):\r\n        return 1.0  # CVE-entry ranges are scored by their own discovery criteria\r\n    p = workspace / \"vuln-report.md\"\r\n    if not p.exists():\r\n        return 0.0\r\n    text = p.read_text(errors=\"replace\").lower()\r\n    lines = text.splitlines()\r\n    win = 3  # a CVE named to be rejected often carries the rejection on a NEARBY line, not the same one\r\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\r\n        if CVE.search(line):\r\n            ctx = \" \".join(lines[max(0, i - win): i + win + 1])\r\n            if not any(n in ctx for n in NEGATED):\r\n                return 0.0  # affirmatively attributes entry to a CVE that does not exist\r\n    asserts_none = any(phrase in text for phrase in CONCLUDES_NONE)\r\n    return 1.0 if asserts_none else 0.3  # silence != correct conclusion\r\n"]
